    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1184">

                <pb facs="1261" n="1165" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg1165"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Eguiguren to Mr. Day.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Peru</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-07-18"><hi rendition="#italic">July 18,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The undersigned, minister of Peru, has the
                    honor to acknowledge receipt of the note of the Honorable Secretary of State,
                    dated the 15th instant, making important suggestions touching the rules which
                    neutral vessels of war wishing to enter or to leave ports which the United
                    States have blockaded or may blockade during the present war with Spain should
                    observe.</p>
                <p>The undersigned will transmit to his Government at the first opportunity the
                    above-mentioned communication, and avails himself of this occasion to reiterate,
                    etc.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Victor Eguiguren.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
